  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A binary operation * is defined by a * b = √(a + 4b). (a) Find 1 * 2. (b) Determine whether * is commutative."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: A binary operation is just a recipe: put the left number where a is and the right number where b is."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p057_q01.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p057-q01 from workbook page 57."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Substitute a = 1, b = 2 into √(a + 4b).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "1 + 4(2) = 1 + 8 = 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 1 * 2 = √9 = 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Write down what commutative would require.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "a * b = b * a for every pair of values"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Need √(a + 4b) = √(b + 4a)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Test the reversed pair 2 * 1.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 + 4(1) = 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2 * 1 = √6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Compare the two results.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "3 is not equal to √6, which is about 2.45"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: * is not commutative"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Substitute a = 1 and b = 2 into the rule for part (a); for part (b) compare a * b with b * a using the same pair of numbers."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) 1 * 2 = 3  (b) * is not commutative, since 1 * 2 = 3 but 2 * 1 = √6, and 3 is not equal to √6"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "In a * b = √(a + 4b) the two inputs are treated differently: b is multiplied by 4 while a is not, so swapping them changes the value. To prove an operation is not commutative you only need one counter-example; to prove it is commutative you must show it algebraically for all a and b."
    }
  ],
